# Sun Sports — project architecture

## Package and entry

- App package name: `sun_sports`. Imports: `package:sun_sports/...`
- Entry: `lib/main.dart` → `ProviderScope` + `App` (`lib/app.dart`)

## Directory layout

- **`lib/core/`** — cross-cutting: theme, breakpoints, router shell, errors (`Failure`, `ServerException`), logging, websocket stack, sport/game API clients, shared repositories under `core/services/repositories`, pagination helpers
- **`lib/features/<feature>/`** — feature modules; typical split:
  - `data/` — datasources, `*_impl` repositories, DTOs (`*.freezed.dart` alongside)
  - `domain/` — entities, repository interfaces, use cases, Riverpod providers/notifiers, freezed state
  - `presentation/` — screens/widgets; often subdivided `mobile/`, `tablet/`, `desktop/`
- **`lib/shared/`** — reusable UI, responsive helpers, profile navigation shell, enums

## Data and errors

- Repositories return **`Future<Either<Failure, T>>`** (`dartz`) in the style of `AuthRepositoryImpl`
- Map API models ↔ domain entities in repository/data layer; keep widgets free of JSON parsing
- Use **`Failure`** / **`ServerException`** from `lib/core/error/` for consistent error handling

## State management

- **flutter_riverpod** only (no get_it). Prefer `ConsumerWidget` / `ConsumerStatefulWidget`; `ref.watch` for rebuilds, `ref.read` for one-off actions / inside listeners
- Complex feature state: **`StateNotifier`** + `StateNotifierProvider` or dedicated notifiers under `domain/notifiers/`

## Routing

- Top-level: **`GoRouter`** in `lib/core/router/app_router.dart` (`MaterialApp.router`)
- In-shell navigation (tabs, profile stack): **`Navigator.pushNamed`** / `MaterialPageRoute` patterns (see `ProfileRouter`, `MainShellLayout`)

## Responsive UI

- **`DeviceType`**: `mobile`, `tablet`, `desktop`, `largeDesktop` (`lib/shared/domain/enums/responsive_enums.dart`)
- **`Breakpoints`** in `lib/core/constants/breakpoints.dart` — use **`ResponsiveBuilder.getDeviceType(context)`** or **`ResponsiveBuilder.responsive(...)`** (`lib/shared/responsive/responsive_builder.dart`)
- Split presentation by breakpoint folders when behavior diverges (`mobile/` vs `desktop/`)

## Local packages

- `packages/sport_socket` — protobuf / websocket sport feed
- `packages/adaptive_overlay`, `packages/flutter_slider_drawer` — UI utilities  
Do not duplicate their behavior in app code; extend or wrap in `shared/` if needed.

## Design references

- Figma links and node-ids appear in widget comments; preserve them when touching implemented screens
